# No auto-merge; watch every check

Never enable auto-merge. Do not pass `--auto`, call the auto-merge API, or
turn auto-merge on in the UI.

"Autopilot", "babysit", "watch until green", and "merge when green" mean you
watch the pull request yourself. Wait until every attached check has finished
and succeeded. Required-check lists and branch protection do not define that
set. A repository may allow a merge while important checks are still running.

Skip a check only with a high-confidence reason it does not apply, and say
why. Merge only after that wait, and only when the user asked you to merge.
